From: j7
Subject: j7 fb: paint a real wallpaper and stop rewriting duplicate rows

The swap records carry one opaque desktop layer and no wallpaper, so the pixels have to

be supplied: a raw BGRA image at the logical display size is read once from the data

volume (j7wall=<path>, default /var/mobile/j7wall.raw) and painted wherever the desktop

is wide-run opaque black or fully transparent. The gradient stays as the fallback.

1334 logical rows over 1920 panel rows means 586 panel rows are exact copies of the row

above; they are now skipped instead of stored again.

Co-Authored-By: dipa-studio <183933817+dipa-studio@users.noreply.github.com>

